    <h2>Is it actually an emergency?</h2>
    <p><strong>Call right now, any hour:</strong> a burst pipe you can't isolate, water coming through a ceiling or light fitting, sewage backing up into the house, no water at all, or a gas smell (leave the house first, then call from outside).</p>
    <p><strong>It can wait until morning — and cost you less:</strong> a dripping tap, one slow drain, a toilet that still flushes with a bucket, a relief valve dribble. We'll book you the first business-hours slot and you keep the after-hours fee in your pocket. We tell you this on the phone too.</p>
