    <h2>Three things to do right now</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><h3>Kill the water</h3><p>Find the toby — the small lid at your front boundary — and turn the valve clockwise. Can't budge it? There's usually a second valve where the pipe enters the house.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><h3>Kill the power to wet areas</h3><p>If water is anywhere near wiring or light fittings, flip the affected circuits off at the switchboard. Don't stand in water to do it.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><h3>Open the lowest tap</h3><p>An outside tap or laundry tap on the ground floor drains the pipes and takes the pressure off the leak fast.</p></div>
    </div>
